{
  "requirement": "Saved configuration MUST remain distinct from resolved runtime configuration.\nSerializing and deserializing a valid configuration MUST preserve its semantic\nvalues, including explicit versus omitted settings. Optional fields MAY be\nomitted on serialization; defaults and environment-derived values MUST NOT be\nmaterialized into omitted fields. TOML comments and formatting need not\nround-trip.\n\nLoading configuration or running a configured feature MUST NOT rewrite the user\nor project configuration as a side effect. Resolved credentials and live runtime\nobjects MUST NOT enter the serialized data structures. Explicitly supplied\ncredential values are permitted only in the fields documented by the authoring\nfeature; credentials resolved from a profile or environment MUST NOT be written\nback to configuration.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment:** the requirement is met. The implementation is marked and complete, and the tests cover the main cases.\n\n## Implementation\n\n**Saved versus resolved configuration**\n- The saved types in `src/config.rs` are `UserConfig`, `WorkspaceConfig` and their nested structs. They derive `Serialize` and `Deserialize`.\n- `ResolvedAuthoringConfig` does not derive `Serialize`. It holds only the selected saved values (the source path, the name, and a clone of `BackendConfig`). Resolved runtime objects such as the rig client are created in `providers.rs` and never stored in a config type.\n\n**Round-trip fidelity**\n- Optional fields use `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = ...)]`. This applies to `concurrency`, `endpoint`, `api_key_env`, `aws_profile`, `region`, `credentials` and `options`.\n- Omitted settings stay omitted. For example, `OllamaConfig::endpoint()` supplies the default URL only at read time, and the stored field stays `None`. The same holds for `ResolvedAuthoringConfig::effective_concurrency()`.\n- `UserAuthoringConfig::configs` has no skip, so an explicit empty `configs = {}` is preserved.\n- `UserConfig::to_toml` and `WorkspaceConfig::to_toml` validate the value and then serialize it. `parse` and `load_*` use the same `decode` and `validate` path. All of these functions are marked `{impl}` for this requirement.\n\n**No rewriting as a side effect**\n- A search of `src/` finds no code that writes `habeas.toml` or the user config file.\n- `to_toml` only returns a `String`, and `load_user_config` / `load_workspace_config` only read.\n- `configured_assessment` writes only evidence and usage files.\n\n**Credentials**\n- Explicit credentials exist only in the documented fields: Bedrock `credentials` and Ollama `api_key`, held in `SecretString`. `deny_unknown_fields` rejects them anywhere else.\n- `SecretString`'s `Debug` output is redacted, and `decode` scrubs secrets from error messages.\n- `OllamaConfig::api_key_from` returns a plain `String` and does not store it back. The environment-derived value never enters the serialized structures.\n\n## Tests (`tests/configuration.rs`)\n\n- `absent_and_minimal_configuration_are_distinct_and_read_only` checks that absent and minimal configs differ, that the file is unchanged after loading, and that the config round-trips.\n- `backend_configuration_round_trips_without_materializing_defaults` checks that the serialized form contains no `endpoint` or `concurrency`, and that arbitrary options round-trip.\n- `authoring_concurrency_defaults_overrides_and_invalid_values` checks that a default is not written, an explicit value is, and invalid values are rejected.\n- `ollama_authentication_resolves_separately_and_rejects_missing_values` checks that the serialized form contains the env var name and not the resolved value.\n- `workspace_discovery_uses_nearest_file_without_merging_or_rewriting_it` checks that the workspace file is byte-identical after loading, and that serialization omits empty maps and round-trips.\n- `explicit_credentials_round_trip_but_diagnostics_and_debug_redact_them` covers explicit credentials round-tripping, redaction, and invalid forms.\n- `user_and_workspace_authoring_tables_round_trip_every_map` covers `projects`, empty `configs`, and nested `options`.\n- `workspace_defaults_and_configs_combine_with_existing_user_selections` is a further test marked for this requirement.\n\n## Minor observations (not gaps)\n\n- `OllamaConfig::api_key` and `providers.rs::connect` resolve credentials into the client. `api_key` is marked for this requirement. `connect` is marked only for `authoring.credentials`, and it does not violate the requirement.\n- No test runs a full configured feature and then checks that the config files are unchanged. This is acceptable because no config-writing code path exists.\n- Explicit empty `options = {}` or workspace `configs = {}` collapse to omitted. The requirement allows this (\"Optional fields MAY be omitted\"), and the values are semantically equal.",
